{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792402912,"nonce":"vuD4/YO1+p1DlpBprLLcdVSVgTY=","title":"Settings: Install and Remove buttons of the custom themes row are different heights","message":"User report with a screenshot (2026-10-19). `#rayde-theme-install` had `class=\"rayde-add\"` (height 32) and `#rayde-theme-remove` had none (26), beside a 32 px input.\n\nAlso found: the Theme Studio's role chips used the class `rayde-chip`, which the Build, Extension and Library settings already use for their buttons, so the Studio's border, colour and radius rules restyled those buttons. Renamed to `rayde-role-chip`.\n\nFix: Remove takes `rayde-add`; the chip class is renamed. `tests/Snapshots.hx` gets `sameHeight`, which fails when controls on one row differ: the custom themes row, the Studio header, the font and stylesheet add rows. Verified it fails on the old markup (26 against 32).","files":null}]}